    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Cimmerians were culturally and archaeologically indistinguishable from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a>, yet every source of their own time treated them as a separate people.</li><li>After crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> they defeated Urartu, destroyed the empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phrygia">Phrygia</a>, sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a> and for a time ended Neo-Assyrian control in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, helping the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydians">Lydians</a> rise.</li><li>Around c. 635 BC the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madyes">Madyes</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydians">Lydians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alyattes">Alyattes</a> defeated them, and they disappeared from history, assimilated by the peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>By 657 BC an Assyrian astrologer was calling the Cimmerian king Dugdammî šar-kiššati, '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-the-universe">King of the Universe</a>', a title normally held only by the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and given to no other foreign ruler in the empire's history.</p></aside>
    </section>

